 "tags": [
  {
   "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Managed Service for Apache Kafka API (v1) discovery document. Every other official method returns HTTP 501 UNIMPLEMENTED. Clusters, topics and Connect clusters are configuration metadata: no Kafka broker, bootstrap address, partition, message, consumer group, connector or network endpoint exists, and clusters report ACTIVE immediately. Capacity is validated against the documented minimums (3 vCPUs, 3 GiB, 1 to 8 GiB per vCPU) but nothing is provisioned; view=FULL returns no broker details or Kafka version. Topic partition counts cannot be changed by the simulator, Connect cluster kafkaCluster references are not resolved, and the reserved Connect worker config is refused. Delete topics before their cluster: deleting a cluster that still has topics fails with FAILED_PRECONDITION. ACLs, consumer groups, connectors and schema registries are unimplemented.",
   "name": "Managed Service for Apache Kafka"
  }
 ],
